    "done_when": "A dispatch from the fleet allocation (host 98dci4-clu-2018) for project reckon is refused with \"watch producer for reckon did not release its seat within 30s; arming stopped\". The reckon watch producer is registered on the login node 98dci4-srv-1006 (registration host field, parent_pid 877173). watch_observer_alive in reckon/crew/runs.py checks parent_pid against the LOCAL process table without comparing hosts, so from any other host it returns False. _ensure_watch_producer in reckon/crew/dispatch.py then tries to unwatch a producer it cannot signal and times out. _record_producer_dead and _seat_names_a_foreign_host in the same module already hold the right rule: a seat naming another host is never dead from here.\n\n1. watch_observer_alive returns None, meaning unknown, for a registration naming a foreign host, so arming leaves a live foreign producer alone. A registration naming this host, or naming no host, keeps today's behaviour.\n2. Test in tests/test_watch_observer_is_host_aware.py: a registration whose host is another name and whose parent_pid is not alive locally reads None, and _ensure_watch_producer with that registration and a fresh seat does not call _stop_watch_producer_within. A same-host registration with a dead parent still reads False.\n\nGate: tests/test_watch_observer_is_host_aware.py, tests/test_arm_lock_is_never_held_by_a_follower.py, and every tests/ file that imports watch_observer_alive, watch_state or _ensure_watch_producer. Build that list from the head tree with grep -l. Run with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, one log each for base and head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta.",
